00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:10.480
the weekend. Just coincidentally, a lot of&nbsp;
wild stuff happened at it. And one of those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:16.320
things was the organization of gay Republicans&nbsp;
called the Log Cabin Republicans got banned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:22.720
from having a booth at the convention, so they&nbsp;
were no longer allowed to show up at as an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:26.800
organization. Obviously, I'm sure individuals&nbsp;
could have still gone, but because they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:32.160
represented a gay representation organization,&nbsp;
they were not allowed to set up their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:37.200
normal booth. A group of Texas Republicans who&nbsp;
represent conservatives and the LGBTQ community&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.360
said they were denied the ability to set up a&nbsp;
booth at the Texas Republican Party Convention.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.280
The Log Cabin Republicans of Fort Worth, a&nbsp;
chapter of the National Log Cabin Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:49.280
Organization, said they were not allowed to set&nbsp;
up a booth at the convention, which took place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:53.760
